-- Backfill book_dna.narrator_cast for already-tagged books, catalog-wide.
-- Tier A field (ordinary metadata, not a judgment call) that a stale
-- skill instruction silently excluded from every tagging batch until
-- 2026-09-21 (see docs/project-log.md's 2026-09-21 entries and
-- .claude/skills/tag-catalog-batch/SKILL.md's narrator_cast section) --
-- this migration is the mechanical, one-pass fix for the 1157+ books
-- tagged before that fix landed, using the same derivation rule new
-- batches now apply per-book:
--   * an audiobook_editions row with edition_type = 'dramatized_full_cast'
--     -> 'full_cast' (regardless of that row's own narrator count)
--   * else a 'standard' row with exactly 1 narrator -> 'single_narrator',
--     exactly 2 -> 'dual_narrator'
--   * a 'standard' row with 3+ narrators, or a book with both a 1-narrator
--     and a 2-narrator 'standard' edition (genuinely different narrations,
--     ambiguous which one 'the' narrator_cast should describe) has no clean
--     enum value -- left NULL, not forced, per the skill's own rule
--   * no audiobook_editions row at all -- left NULL (the common case)
--
-- Every UPDATE scoped by (title, author) -- verified against the live
-- catalog first that none of these 739 candidates hit a duplicate
-- (title, author) pair (zero such collisions exist catalog-wide as of
-- this migration).
--
-- Coverage: 97 full_cast, 569 single_narrator,
-- 73 dual_narrator (739 total real values set).
-- 56 left NULL as genuinely ambiguous (3+ narrators on a
-- standard edition, or mixed single/dual-narrator editions of the same
-- book) -- flagged as a real vocabulary gap in docs/schema/book-dna.md's
-- tracker, not silently dropped. The remaining tagged books have no
-- audiobook_editions row yet and correctly stay NULL (nothing to derive).

